WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.674 --> 00:00:08.222
My name is Kiki Vandeweghe.

00:00:08.222 --> 00:00:13.261
I'm the Executive Vice President
of Global Basketball for the NBA.

00:00:13.261 --> 00:00:17.824
[SOUND] I went to UCLA,
it was a fantastic basketball school, and

00:00:17.824 --> 00:00:22.996
I was very, very lucky that I got
drafted by the NBA right out of college.

00:00:22.996 --> 00:00:27.038
Playing for the Denver Nuggets, for
the Portland Trail Blazers, and

00:00:27.038 --> 00:00:30.118
the New York Knicks, and
was kind of a player coach for

00:00:30.118 --> 00:00:33.362
my last year in the league for
the Los Angeles Clippers.

00:00:33.362 --> 00:00:36.510
And after that, ran a couple businesses,

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:40.891
then I got a call to come and
oversee basketball for the NBA.

00:00:40.891 --> 00:00:46.350
And I'm in charge of the games and
everything you see on a basketball court.

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.400
I was at the NBA for about a year.

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.715
Adam Silver was just taking over as the
commissioner, and he really wanted me to

00:00:52.715 --> 00:00:57.635
expand my knowledge, my management skills,
my leadership skills.

00:00:57.635 --> 00:00:58.845
And so he said,

00:00:58.845 --> 00:01:02.375
see if there's a management
program that makes sense for you.

00:01:02.375 --> 00:01:05.735
It was actually really easy once I
found out that Stanford had one.

00:01:07.055 --> 00:01:12.445
At Stanford, you are instructed by
Nobel Prize-winning professors.

00:01:12.445 --> 00:01:17.680
They interact with you in a way that
you could never get any place else.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.610
When you come to ELD,
you come to make yourself better, and

00:01:21.610 --> 00:01:24.510
you come to accelerate your growth curve.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:29.260
And all these things are about
your path and focused on that.

00:01:29.260 --> 00:01:33.090
What you get out of it is
the ability to make others better.

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:35.780
That's what I'm able to do in my job.

00:01:35.780 --> 00:01:37.040
Make other players better,

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:42.270
give them some insight, make the NBA
league office a bit of a better place.

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:47.300
And bring in some new ideas that perhaps
can make not only basketball, but

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:53.160
the way we bring basketball to our fans
around the world, a better experience.

00:01:53.160 --> 00:01:55.220
I have changed rules
a little bit at the NBA.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:59.640
I was first hired as a Vice President,
a little bit more limited role.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.515
Actually after this program,

00:02:01.515 --> 00:02:05.923
I was made the Executive Vice President
in charge of all the basketball.

00:02:05.923 --> 00:02:08.671
I really do think that this
program had a lot to do with that.

00:02:08.671 --> 00:02:12.801
ELD is a game changer for
anybody who wants to engage, and

00:02:12.801 --> 00:02:15.821
wants to work, and wants to understand.

00:02:15.821 --> 00:02:19.099
And what you need to bring
to the table is a curiosity.

00:02:19.099 --> 00:02:24.380
ELD exceeded every expectation
that I could potentially have had.

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:28.205
I recommended that anybody who wants
to not only make themselves and

00:02:28.205 --> 00:02:32.920
their career path better but accelerate
the career path of anybody they work with.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:37.104
Would do well to come
here to an ELD program.

00:02:37.104 --> 00:02:38.382
[MUSIC]

